# GTM Documentation

- Keep positioning, pitch, hiring, onboarding, retrospective, and vertical 1-pagers under `docs/gtm/`.
- Market cost/TAM figures are framing for discovery only — not Ghost Fabric measured outcomes.
- Never imply FedRAMP/SOC2/NERC certification until earned; readiness stubs live under `docs/compliance/`.
- Pilot language stays simulation-first with human approval and synthetic or approved data.
- Hiring tasks remain blocked until humans post roles, score interviews, sign offers, and confirm starts; repository JDs and scorecards are preparation evidence only.
- A customer pilot requires signed commercial/data agreements, named customer owners, approved deployment/data scope, and a recorded go/no-go; never commit customer evidence or credentials.
